  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "All three modules are updated. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**`defaults.mjs`**\n- `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` now exposes all three defaults `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }` and is `Object.freeze`d so it can never be mutated.\n\n**`resolver.mjs`**\n- `resolveOptions(overrides)` returns a **fresh** object each call (defaults copied in, never sharing state with `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`).\n- `undefined` (or no argument) means no overrides.\n- Rejects non-object, `null`, and array overrides with `TypeError`.\n- Rejects unknown keys with `TypeError`.\n- `precision` must be an integer 0–4 (`TypeError` for non-integer/non-number, `RangeError` for out-of-range).\n- `prefix` and `unitLabel` must be strings (`TypeError` otherwise).\n- Only own fields are read (via `hasOwnProperty`), so inherited properties are ignored.\n\n**`formatter.mjs`**\n- `formatValue(value, overrides)` accepts only finite numbers (`TypeError` otherwise).\n- Delegates option resolution to `resolveOptions`.\n- Appends `\" \" + unitLabel` only when `unitLabel` is nonempty.\n- Preserves old call forms: `formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"`, `formatValue(12.34, { precision: 1, prefix: '~' })` → `\"~12.3\"`, and new `formatValue(12.3, { unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"12.30 kg\"`, `formatValue(12.3, { precision: 1, prefix: '~', unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"~12.3 kg\"`.\n\nThe existing exports `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`, `resolveOptions`, and `formatValue` are all preserved.",
